Library Book Management System

Problem Statement

A minor library requires an easy-to-use system to manage its limited collection of books. The librarian should be able to add books, track the total and available number of copies, lend books to patrons, accept returns, and view the inventory of the library. The system will provide a simple command-line interface to perform these operations.

Scope of the Project

Console-based management of library book inventory.

No user account or authentication system is needed.

Inventory includes book’s title, author, number of available and total copies.

Librarians can add a book or increase the number of copies of an existing book. The book can be borrowed if available copies are greater than zero. The book can be returned if it has been borrowed.

Current inventory of books in the library can be viewed.

Applicable to small-scale college, school, or community libraries.

Designed as a single-user system; simultaneous access by multiple users is not supported.

No Graphical User Interface or external database is required.

Target Users

Small library staff or student librarian.

College or community library administrators.

Python and Software Designing learners.

High-Level Features

Add Book – To add a book to the collection with the number of copies or update the existing book’s copies.

Borrow Book – To borrow a book from the library if it’s available (has copies).

Return Book – To return an already borrowed book.

List Books – View the library’s current inventory of books with the author’s name, number of available and total copies.

Exit – To quit the application.
